 Channel Extension, including H.264/AVC420 and AVC444 video streaming support.
 
+## Platform H.264 decoders
+
+A client can also decode AVC420 outside the channel processor, with a decoder that is asynchronous or lives
+elsewhere (a browser's WebCodecs `VideoDecoder`, a hardware decoder): `GraphicsPipelineClient::with_external_h264`
+hands each frame out (`take_h264_frames`) and applies its pixels, in order, when they come back
+(`complete_h264_frame`); commands after it and its frame acknowledgement wait until then. AVC444 is handed out as
+its YUV420 main view (the auxiliary view is decoded but not shown), so such a client can advertise the V10
+capability sets, the only ones Windows streams H.264 to. The `h264` module prepares
+the bitstream for such decoders (Annex B, and an SPS that declares output in decoding order, without which conformant
+decoders hold every picture back).
+
